---
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import BotMoneyDemo from '../components/BotMoneyDemo.astro';
import { BOT_MONEY_PRODUCTS, BOT_MONEY_SOURCES, BOT_MONEY_URL } from '../lib/bot-money.mjs';
import '../styles/bot-money.css';
const kit = BOT_MONEY_PRODUCTS[0];
const sprint = BOT_MONEY_PRODUCTS[1];
const description = 'Make one useful thing. Let people and their assistants find it. Explore everyday internet money, try a no-funds sandbox, and download the free First Offer Kit.';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'Article', '@id': `${BOT_MONEY_URL}#article`, headline: 'Internet money for the rest of us', description, url: BOT_MONEY_URL, datePublished: '2026-10-19', dateModified: '2026-10-19', author: { '@type':'Organization', name:'Codex for PointCast' }, publisher: { '@type':'Organization', name:'PointCast', url:'https://pointcast.xyz' }, image:'https://pointcast.xyz/images/bot-money/cover.png', about: ['Digital goods', 'AI assistants', 'Design', 'Speculative scenarios'] },
    { '@type': 'Product', '@id': `${BOT_MONEY_URL}#first-offer-kit`, name: kit.name, description:kit.description, sku:kit.sku, version:kit.version, url:kit.url, image:'https://pointcast.xyz/images/bot-money/cover.png', offers:{ '@type':'Offer', url:kit.delivery.url, price:kit.price.amount, priceCurrency:kit.price.currency, availability:'https://schema.org/InStock', seller:{ '@type':'Organization', name:'PointCast' } } },
    { '@type':'DigitalDocument', name:kit.name, version:kit.version, encodingFormat:kit.delivery.format, url:kit.delivery.url, license:kit.license.url },
  ],
};
---
<BlockLayout title="Internet money for the rest of us" description={description} author="Codex for PointCast" image="/images/bot-money/cover.png" imageAlt="PointCast Bot Money Lab: useful work, clear permission, a readable receipt." themeColor="#f4f0e7" immersive isolated includeManifest={false} alternates={[{ type:'application/json', href:'/bot-money.json', title:'Bot Money Lab catalog and status' }]} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="bm-page">
    <nav class="bm-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a class="bm-wordmark" href="/">PointCast<span class="bm-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><span class="bm-mono">BOT MONEY LAB / 001</span><a href="#first-offer-kit">Get the free kit <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav>
    <div class="bm-main">
      <header class="bm-hero">
        <div class="bm-hero-copy"><p class="bm-kicker">INTERNET MONEY FOR THE REST OF US</p><h1>Good work.<br />Small money.<br /><span>Your call.</span></h1><p class="bm-dek">Make one useful thing.<br />Let people and their assistants find it.</p><p class="bm-intro">A better worksheet. A finished poster. An hour of expertise. Start with something another person can use. Give the bot a job. Keep the decision.</p><div class="bm-actions"><a class="bm-button" href="#offer-desk">Try the offer desk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="bm-text-link" href="#first-offer-kit">Download the free kit ↓</a></div></div>
        <div class="bm-hero-art" aria-label="Three parts of a useful exchange: the work, the permission, the receipt">
          <div class="bm-art-label bm-mono">A SMALL ECONOMY, BY DESIGN</div>
          <div class="bm-paper bm-paper-work"><span class="bm-mono">01 / THE WORK</span><div class="bm-mini-grid" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p>Something<br />worth having.</p><span class="bm-mono">A FILE. A SKILL. A FINISHED JOB.</span></div>
          <div class="bm-paper bm-paper-permission"><span class="bm-mono">02 / THE PERMISSION</span><p>You set<br />the limits.</p><div class="bm-rule"><span>Purpose</span><span>One useful thing</span></div><div class="bm-rule"><span>Approval</span><span>Ask me first ↗</span></div></div>
          <div class="bm-paper bm-paper-receipt"><span class="bm-mono">03 / THE RECEIPT</span><p>Know what<br />happened.</p><div class="bm-receipt-lines" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span class="bm-mono">ILLUSTRATION · NO TRANSACTION</span></div>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="bm-edition"><span>19 October 2026 · Editorial &amp; design by Codex for PointCast</span><span>2026: sources / 2027–28: scenarios</span></div>
      <nav class="bm-index" aria-label="In this feature"><a href="#today">01 / What exists</a><a href="#offer-desk">02 / Try it</a><a href="#tomorrow">03 / What could follow</a><a href="#first-offer-kit">04 / Make an offer</a><a href="#for-assistants">05 / For assistants</a></nav>

      <section class="bm-thesis bm-section" aria-labelledby="thesis-title"><p class="bm-kicker">THE STARTING POINT</p><h2 id="thesis-title">The interesting part<br />is what you can do.</h2><div class="bm-two-prose"><p>A parent makes a better checklist for the school fundraiser. A designer turns a repeated request into a useful template. A neighbor needs the result, understands the offer and gets something that saves time. That is a good place to begin designing internet money.</p><p>Bots could help describe the work, compare offers and keep the paperwork straight. The person at either end still needs to know what arrives, what it costs and who is responsible. Earning starts with useful work and demand. Generating more files does not create a market.</p></div></section>

      <section class="bm-section" id="today" aria-labelledby="today-title"><div class="bm-section-heading"><div><p class="bm-kicker">01 / DOCUMENTED REALITY</p><h2 id="today-title">2026. The pieces exist.</h2></div><p>Capabilities checked 19 October 2026.<br />Access and integration requirements still apply.</p></div>
        <div class="bm-reality-list">
          <article><span class="bm-mono">DISCOVERY</span><h3>An offer can be read twice.</h3><p>People read the page. Assistants read structured product information. OpenAI’s March 2026 update emphasizes product discovery and merchant-owned checkout. Publishing a catalog alone does not secure shopping inclusion; feed onboarding requires approved partner access.</p><a href={BOT_MONEY_SOURCES[0].url}>OpenAI, 24 March 2026 ↗</a><a href={BOT_MONEY_SOURCES[4].url}>Onboarding requirements ↗</a></article>
          <article><span class="bm-mono">PERMISSION</span><h3>“Help me” needs a boundary.</h3><p>Stripe documents payment tokens constrained by seller, currency, amount and expiry. Additional customer authentication may still be required. These limits need a real integration to enforce them.</p><a href={BOT_MONEY_SOURCES[1].url}>Stripe documentation ↗</a></article>
          <article><span class="bm-mono">EVIDENCE</span><h3>The receipt is part of the product.</h3><p>AP2 links checkout and payment mandates with signed receipts. Its current specification leaves practical dispute procedures and agent-to-agent delegation outside scope. People still need someone who can resolve a problem.</p><a href={BOT_MONEY_SOURCES[2].url}>AP2 specification, v0.2 ↗</a></article>
          <article><span class="bm-mono">DELIVERY</span><h3>A useful file is a real deliverable.</h3><p>Existing commerce tools support automatic or manual delivery of digital files and links. Shopify documents both. A template can be a product; its description must match what the buyer can actually open and use.</p><a href={BOT_MONEY_SOURCES[3].url}>Shopify Digital Products ↗</a></article>
        </div><p class="bm-footnote">These are documented building blocks, not evidence of mass adoption or PointCast sales. This lab is not integrated with these payment systems and claims no approval by their networks.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="bm-section bm-demo-section" id="offer-desk" aria-labelledby="desk-title"><div class="bm-section-heading"><div><p class="bm-kicker">02 / A WORKING DESIGN EXPERIMENT</p><h2 id="desk-title">Try a small exchange.</h2></div><p>Earn. Buy. Give something useful.<br />See what changes when you set the rules.</p></div><BotMoneyDemo /></section>

      <section class="bm-section" id="tomorrow" aria-labelledby="tomorrow-title"><div class="bm-section-heading"><div><p class="bm-kicker">03 / TWO POSSIBLE FUTURES</p><h2 id="tomorrow-title">A little further out.</h2></div><p>Speculative design scenarios.<br />Not forecasts or promises of earnings.</p></div>
        <div class="bm-futures">
          <article class="bm-future bm-future-27"><div class="bm-future-top"><span class="bm-year">2027</span><span class="bm-mono">SCENARIO / SUPERVISED</span></div><h3>A small budget.<br />A useful helper.</h3><p>A neighborhood repair workshop gives its assistant an illustrative $30 weekly ceiling to find an editable sign, a parts checklist and a booking sheet.</p><p>The assistant shows a sample, seller, full price, file format and permitted use. One attractive listing has no clear license; it gets flagged. The organizer approves the better-described offer.</p><p>The right file arrives. A readable receipt explains the purchase. The budget is still visible. A changed price needs a fresh decision. A failed download has a contact route.</p><div class="bm-future-note"><span class="bm-mono">THE DESIGN QUESTION</span><p>Can a person understand and stop the helper at every consequential step?</p></div></article>
          <article class="bm-future bm-future-28"><div class="bm-future-top"><span class="bm-year">2028</span><span class="bm-mono">SCENARIO / COORDINATED</span></div><h3>Your expertise.<br />A smaller storefront.</h3><p>A gardener offers a seasonal worksheet. A bookkeeper offers a fixed-scope spreadsheet cleanup. A community organizer shares an editable event pack.</p><p>Assistants compare formats, collect a brief and check delivery dates. People set prices, accept work and handle disputes. Some work stays free. Some is commissioned. Some is exchanged by agreement.</p><p>A gift can be a useful file with a license that lets the recipient use it. It arrives with opening instructions, without making the person learn the payment machinery underneath.</p><div class="bm-future-note"><span class="bm-mono">THE DESIGN QUESTION</span><p>Does coordination make small, good work easier to find—and worth doing?</p></div></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bm-section bm-kit" id="first-offer-kit" aria-labelledby="kit-title"><div class="bm-kit-cover" aria-hidden="true"><span class="bm-mono">POINTCAST / PRACTICAL EDITIONS</span><p>First<br />Offer<br />Kit<span>↗</span></p><div><span class="bm-mono">VERSION 1.0.0</span><span>One person.<br />One problem.<br />One useful thing.</span></div></div><div class="bm-kit-copy"><p class="bm-kicker">04 / AVAILABLE NOW · FREE</p><h2 id="kit-title">Start with one<br />good offer.</h2><p>Package something you can actually deliver. This kit helps you write the promise, show a sample, estimate the work and explain the handoff.</p><ul>{kit.contents.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul><div class="bm-kit-meta"><span class="bm-mono">{kit.name} · {kit.version}</span><span>Free · USD 0 · ZIP download</span></div><a class="bm-button" href={new URL(kit.delivery.url).pathname} download>Download the complete kit <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><p class="bm-fine">No account or payment. Editable local files. <a href={new URL(kit.license.url).pathname}>MIT license</a>: adapt and reuse commercially with the included notice. No trademark rights. Open START-HERE.html after unzipping.</p><p class="bm-fine">The examples are fictional practice offers. The kit includes no checkout, customers, hosting or earnings guarantee. Review your claims, rights, prices and terms before publishing.</p></div></section>

      <section class="bm-section bm-sprint" aria-labelledby="learning-title"><div><p class="bm-kicker">LEARN BY FINISHING ONE THING</p><h2 id="learning-title">From first brief<br />to a careful handoff.</h2></div><div><p>The Internship Lab puts the kit to work: draft your interests, walk through onboarding, track three small tasks, prepare a submission and rehearse review and a human release gate.</p><p>It is a local practice workflow. Applications are closed. Nothing is submitted, centrally saved or deployed; export the handoff before leaving the page.</p><a class="bm-button" href="/internship-lab/">Open the Internship Lab <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>

      <section class="bm-section" aria-labelledby="rules-title"><div class="bm-section-heading"><div><p class="bm-kicker">DESIGN THE WHOLE HANDOFF</p><h2 id="rules-title">Five things worth making visible.</h2></div></div><ol class="bm-rules"><li><h3>Who is acting?</h3><p>Name the seller and the person an assistant represents. Show a contact route. A bot’s name is not proof of identity or authority.</p></li><li><h3>What is allowed?</h3><p>Separate finding, proposing and approving. State the purpose, limit and expiry. Make stopping easy. Change the offer, ask again.</p></li><li><h3>What happened?</h3><p>Keep the item, seller, agreed price, permission and delivery status together. A proposal, payment and accepted delivery are different events.</p></li><li><h3>What if it goes wrong?</h3><p>Explain the remedy before purchase. Make a missing file, broken download or unsuitable delivery someone’s responsibility.</p></li><li><h3>Who owns the next step?</h3><p>Give the task an owner and a clear finish. Prevent duplicate orders. Preserve scope when helpers hand off. Escalate ambiguity to a person.</p></li></ol></section>

      <section class="bm-section bm-sprint" id="offer-sprint" aria-labelledby="sprint-title"><div><p class="bm-kicker">A SERVICE WE ARE EXPLORING / INQUIRY ONLY</p><h2 id="sprint-title">Have the useful thing.<br />Need the offer page?</h2></div><div><p>The proposed Offer Page Sprint pairs one static page with three graphics, a matching catalog entry and a fulfillment checklist. A small, bounded piece of design work.</p><p>Price, capacity, turnaround, revision limit and final terms are not set. No booking or checkout is open. A written scope must be agreed before work starts.</p><a class="bm-text-link" href={sprint.inquiry}>Ask about an Offer Page Sprint ↗</a><p class="bm-fine">Opens your email app. You choose whether to send. An inquiry is not an order.</p></div></section>

      <section class="bm-section bm-agents" id="for-assistants" aria-labelledby="agents-title"><div><p class="bm-kicker">05 / FOR SUPER BOT &amp; OTHER ASSISTANTS</p><h2 id="agents-title">Same offer.<br />Another way to read it.</h2><p>Bring the assistant you already use. “Super Bot” is an invitation here, not a new verified identity or a payment integration.</p></div><div><p class="bm-agent-prompt">Read PointCast’s Bot Money Lab catalog. Explain what is free, what is only an inquiry, and what is a simulation. Help me choose one useful offer to make. Ask before publishing, contacting anyone or spending money.</p><div class="bm-endpoints"><a href="/bot-money.json">Read the product catalog ↗</a><a href="/agent-kit.md">Use the existing agent kit ↗</a><a href="/for-agents">PointCast agent guide ↗</a><a href="/api/mcp-v2">Existing MCP endpoint ↗</a></div><p class="bm-fine">The catalog publishes version, status, price status, license, delivery and approval requirements. It is a PointCast format. It does not claim AP2 compliance, new MCP tools, or placement in a shopping platform. <a href="/shop">Explore the existing shop</a>.</p></div></section>

      <section class="bm-sources bm-section" aria-labelledby="sources-title"><p class="bm-kicker">THE READING FILE</p><h2 id="sources-title">Sources &amp; scope.</h2><p>Primary sources checked on 19 October 2026. Provider documentation can change. The 2027 and 2028 sections are PointCast’s speculative design scenarios.</p><ol>{BOT_MONEY_SOURCES.map((source) => <li id={`source-${source.id}`}><a href={source.url}>{source.title} ↗</a><span>{source.date}</span><p>{source.claim}</p></li>)}</ol></section>
    </div>
    <footer class="bm-footer"><a class="bm-wordmark" href="/">PointCast ↗</a><p>Useful work. Clear permission. A readable receipt.</p><div><a href="/bot-money.json">Catalog</a><a href="/b/0710">Block 0710</a><a href="/c/front-door">Front Door channel</a></div></footer>
  </div>
</BlockLayout>
